Strategy Formulation:
1) For item (1), let the tag for i be 0^i 1 (i ≤ k). Define S = ⋃_{i=1}^k { 0^i 1 x : x ∈ Si }. For each i, fix a sparsity polynomial pi(n) with |Si^{=n}| ≤ pi(n). Then for S, |S^{=n}| ≤ Σ_{i=1}^k pi(n − (i+1)) where the shift (i+1) accounts for the tag length; since k is constant and each pi is polynomial, the sum is polynomial, so S is sparse. Define M^S(⟨x,i⟩): form y = 0^i 1 x and query y ∈ S; accept iff yes; this runs in time polynomial in |x| (tag overhead is O(1)).
2) For item (2), show P_bad-angel ⊆ P by computing αn via A(n) in poly(n) time and then running M(x, αn) in poly(n + |αn|) = poly(n); so the composition is poly-time. Show P ⊆ P_bad-angel by choosing αn = ε and M to ignore α; let A(n) output ε in poly-time. Conclude P_bad-angel = P. Therefore NP = P_bad-angel iff P = NP (unknown; believed false).
3) For item (3), given L ∈ P_angel with polynomial p and DTIME TM M such that x ∈ L iff M(x, α|x|) = 1, define:
   - Choose r ≥ deg p and set t(n) = (n+1)^r.
   - For each n and j ∈ [1..p(n)], define s(n, j) as a binary encoding of (n, j) padded to length t(n) (e.g., s(n, j) = 1^n 0 bin(j) 0^{t(n) − (n + 1 + |bin(j)|)}). Let SL = { s(n, j) : αn[j] = 1 }.
   - Sparsity: For any length m, either m ≠ t(n) for all n, in which case |SL^{=m}| = 0, or m = t(n) for a unique n, in which case |SL^{=m}| ≤ p(n) ≤ (n+1)^{deg p} ≤ t(n) = m (since r ≥ deg p); hence |SL^{=m}| ≤ m, a polynomial bound, so SL is sparse.
   - Oracle decider: On input x of length n, reconstruct αn by, for j = 1..p(n), querying s(n, j) ∈ SL to get bit αn[j] (1 if yes, else 0). Then simulate M(x, αn) and output its result. Total time is O(p(n) + poly(n) + time_M(n + p(n))) = poly(n), and the number/length of queries is polynomial.
This finishes all three parts.
