To find the probability \( P(M \geq t) \), where \( M = \max(T_1, \ldots, T_6) \), we first observe that for each tree \( i \), \( T_i \) follows a geometric distribution with success probability \( \frac{1}{2} \). Hence, \( T_i \geq t \) if the sapling is not successfully transformed into a tree before day \( t \). 

The probability that any individual \( T_i \leq t - 1 \) is given by:
\[ P(T_i \leq t - 1) = 1 - 2^{-(t-1)}. \]

Since \( T_i \) is the earliest day on which the transformation is completed, the probability that \( T_i \geq t \) is the complement of the probability that the transformation has been completed before day \( t \):
\[ P(T_i \geq t) = 1 - P(T_i \leq t - 1) = 2^{-(t-1)}. \]

As \( T_1, \ldots, T_6 \) are independent, the probability that all six transformations are completed before day \( t \) is:
\[ P(T_1 < t, \ldots, T_6 < t) = \prod_{i=1}^{6} P(T_i < t) = \left(1 - 2^{-(t-1)}\right)^6. \]

The complement of this probability gives us the probability that at least one tree has not been completed before day \( t \), which is the same as the probability that the maximum \( M \geq t \):
\[ P(M \geq t) = 1 - (1 - 2^{-(t-1)})^6. \]

**Answer:**  
\( P(M \geq t) = 1 - (1 - 2^{-(t-1)})^6 \) for integer \( t \geq 1 \).
