2. Compute H = n(n+1)/2 modulo m by halving the even factor first: with n ≡ -5 and n+1 ≡ -4 (mod m), the even factor is −4, so H ≡ (−4/2)·(−5) = 10 (mod m).
3. Then S ≡ H^2 ≡ 100 (mod m). Combine with S ≡ 17 (mod m): hence 100 ≡ 17 (mod m) ⇒ m | 83.
